        "Summer here is not mild: April and May push past 43 degrees on the Malwa plateau most years, landing right on top of the internal exams many schools run before closing for the break. A session plan that respects this, shorter and sharper rather than long and exhausting, tends to hold up better than one that ignores it.",
        "Layered on top of the ordinary IB and Cambridge or Edexcel calendar (DP finals in May with a November retake option, Cambridge sitting twice a year and Edexcel offering an additional January window) are two entirely local disruptions: Navratri and Diwali both reshape family and hostel schedules across Madhya Pradesh for stretches at a time, and roughly once every twelve years the city hosts the Simhastha gathering, which brings crowds large enough to affect travel and routine city-wide for weeks. The next occurrence, expected near 2028, is worth mapping against an exam date well in advance.",
        "A DP student connected to Ujjain typically feels pressure first around Class 11 internals, then through a run of Internal Assessment deadlines across Class 12, then again when predicted grades get finalised for university applications in the autumn, and finally in the run-up to May mocks. Getting a tutoring plan started as early as April or July of Class 11 buys room to sort out weak spots before any of that stacks up.",
