  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Ujjain?", answer: "Since Ujjain has no IB school of its own, finding IB and IGCSE tutors in Ujjain starts with telling us which Indore school, boarding programme or online curriculum your child follows, plus the subject, level and exam session. We shortlist tutors who teach that exact course and confirm a slot that fits your evening or weekend routine. You take a free trial class online before deciding anything, and we suggest another tutor if the fit is not right." },
    { question: "Are there any IB or IGCSE schools actually inside Ujjain?", answer: "No, honestly, Ujjain does not currently have a school running the IB or Cambridge/Edexcel IGCSE. Families who want either curriculum send a child to a school in Indore, roughly 57 kilometres away, either as a day commuter, a weekly boarder, or by choosing an accredited online international school and staying in Ujjain for everything else. Most Ujjain schools follow the MP Board or CBSE." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Ujjain?", answer: "No. A tutor turning up at your door is something this service offers only inside Gurugram and a limited part of Delhi NCR, nowhere else in the country, Ujjain included. What a Ujjain family gets instead is a proper live class conducted one to one over video, whiteboard shared on screen, run from wherever in India the tutor happens to be sitting. It is real private tuition taken from home, just not delivered by someone walking through your front door." },
    { question: "Which schools near Ujjain should I know about for IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Choithram International School and Daly College, both in central Indore, run the IB Diploma or Cambridge IGCSE, with Daly College also offering boarding places. The Emerald Heights International School in Rau, on Indore's southern edge, runs both the IB Diploma and Cambridge IGCSE. All three sit roughly an hour to ninety minutes from Ujjain by road." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor cost for a family based in Ujjain?", answer: "The fee depends on the programme and level, the subject, session length and the tutor's recent experience with that syllabus, and we confirm it for your specific match before the trial. IB Diploma HL subjects usually cost more than MYP or IGCSE Core support. Since every session runs online, there is no travel cost added regardless of where in India the tutor is based." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit to anything?", answer: "There is, and it comes before any decision gets made, not after. A suggested tutor runs one genuine class on a topic pulled straight from your child's own syllabus, with nothing charged and nothing owed afterward. Once that class is done, the tutor writes up what the opening month would look like, and it is entirely up to you to go ahead with it, ask for a change, or look at a different tutor instead." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a Ujjain student?", answer: "Guidance, yes; drafting the actual submission, never. A tutor can help narrow down a workable research angle, talk through what each grading criterion is genuinely looking for, sanity-check a data-collection method, and mark up a draft with honest comments on where it falls short. The line stops at putting the tutor's own words into a document the student then hands in, since that crosses straight into an academic integrity breach nobody here is willing to risk." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for Ujjain students?", answer: "Coverage runs across the usual six subject groups, with Maths (both Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation), Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management and English A Language and Literature seeing the most enquiries from Ujjain-connected families, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance for whichever subject a student has chosen." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Ujjain, not only the Diploma?", answer: "The whole continuum is covered, not just the final two years. Younger MYP students mostly need help pushing past description into genuine criterion-based analysis, particularly in the sciences, plus steady support building their Year 5 Personal Project. PYP-age children work on reading and writing confidence and early number sense, in shorter sessions that slot easily around a family's own routine." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring genuinely effective for a student with no local IB or IGCSE school nearby?", answer: "It holds up well, arguably better here than in a city with its own international school, precisely because Ujjain has nobody locally who teaches, say, IB Chemistry HL or IGCSE Additional Mathematics. A video call with a shared screen and a tutor talking a student through a problem covers nearly everything an in-room lesson would, and it opens the door to specialists based anywhere rather than a short local list." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for students connected to Ujjain?", answer: "Before a name is ever put forward, we check qualifications, how recently that person has actually taught the subject and level in question, and how they approach guiding assessed coursework. Because Ujjain itself has no supply of such tutors to draw on, we deliberately favour someone with fresh, hands-on experience over a generalist. The trial class is still where a family makes the final call, on evidence rather than a description." },
    { question: "When should a Ujjain family start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally right when the course itself begins, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, which leaves time to shore up basics before internal exams, coursework deadlines and predicted grades all arrive at once. A family starting later, even in the final year or right after a move to a boarding school, can still gain real ground by concentrating on the topics and past papers that carry the most weight." },
    { question: "My child is switching from MP Board or CBSE to IB or IGCSE, often alongside a move to Indore. Can a tutor help?", answer: "This comes up often enough from Ujjain that it is close to routine for us. What usually needs direct teaching is not content, since most switching students already know it, but exam language: understanding precisely what an instruction word like 'evaluate' or 'justify' is asking for, alongside new habits around coursework and Internal Assessment planning. Starting over the summer before both the board switch and any school move take effect gives that the best chance to settle in." },
    { question: "Can sessions be scheduled around boarding-school leave or hostel timings?", answer: "Yes, this is one of the more specific things we plan around for Ujjain families with a child boarding in Indore. Sessions are usually set for weekday evenings after prep, weekends, or defined hostel-leave windows, and we build revision blocks around exam-season leave and festival breaks such as Navratri and Diwali rather than fighting against a fixed hostel routine." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not satisfied with the tutor matched to our child?", answer: "Say so, plainly, and a different tutor gets found. Families hear from us every few weeks to check how things are going, and a mismatch is treated as something to fix immediately rather than something a child should simply put up with. Nothing here is locked into a long contract either, so a session run can be paused or stopped whenever it needs to be, at no cost." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Indore school, Vikram University, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "It is not. This is a standalone tutoring service with no formal tie to any school in Indore or Ujjain, to Vikram University, or to the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Any school named on this page is mentioned purely to show where families actually study, and a tutor works strictly to that school's own timetable and the relevant board's published syllabus, nothing more." },
  ],

